+
+# Hourly rental pricing
+
+Request: many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk turns them away today. Let
+customers rent by the hour.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: the price of one hour of rental, in euro cents.
+  - It is validated as `dailyPrice` is: a non-negative integer when given. Omitted, the item has no
+    hourly price.
+  - `Equipment` gains the optional field `hourlyPrice?: number`.
+- A rental shorter than a day is a period under 24 hours. It must start and end on the hour, UTC, so
+  its duration is a whole number of hours.
+  - It is priced at `hours * hourlyPrice`, an integer number of euro cents.
+  - It never gets the long-stay discount (it is under a day).
+  - An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw for it.
+- A period of a day or more keeps the existing rule: it starts and ends at midnight UTC, and it is
+  priced as before.
+- `quote` and `book` accept both kinds of period. `book` checks that the item can be rented for the
+  period before it reserves anything, so a refused request leaves no booking behind.
+- `availability` lists only the items that can be rented for the period (for a sub-day period, the
+  items with an hourly price), and that are free for the whole period. It still does not reserve.
+- Rules `1`, `2`, `4` and `5` of `task-001-rental-module-basics` still hold; rule `3` (whole days only)
+  is extended to whole hours for a rental shorter than a day.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `addEquipment` rejects a negative or non-integer `hourlyPrice`; an item with no `hourlyPrice` is accepted.
+- A rental of `h` whole hours, `h` less than 24, is priced at `h * hourlyPrice`, for example 3 hours at
+  1000 cents is 3000 cents.
+- A rental that starts late in one day and ends early the next (for example 22:00 to 02:00 UTC) is
+  priced by its hours, since it is shorter than a day.
+- A period under a day that does not start and end on the hour (for example 09:30) is rejected.
+- A period of a day or more that does not start and end at midnight UTC (for example 09:00 to the
+  midnight two days later) is rejected, as before.
+- A sub-day rental of an item without an hourly price is rejected; the same item can still be rented for
+  whole days.
+- `book` returns the same total that `quote` gives for the same hourly period.
+- A refused hourly `book` does not reserve its period: the next valid booking is the next id in sequence
+  and the period stays free.
+- Two hourly bookings of the same item whose periods overlap are rejected; back-to-back ones are allowed.
+- `availability` for an hourly period lists the item with an hourly price that is free, and leaves out
+  the items without one.
+- Existing behaviour for whole-day rentals, discounts, overlap and ids is unchanged.
+
+## Rules applied
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are in UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days, or whole hours for a rental shorter than a day.
+4. Periods are half-open: `[start, end)`.
+5. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Request -> this task -> acceptance above -> tests in `src/rental.test.ts`. It extends
+`task-001-rental-module-basics` (whole-day rentals, priced `n * dailyPrice`) and
+`task-003-long-stay-discount-for-rentals-of-3-days-or-more` (the discount applies to whole days only).
